<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Oxybii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 154 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ligurian people of the coast near Fréjus who, with the Deciates, provoked Rome's first intervention beyond the Alps in 154 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known chiefly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>, the Oxybii lived on the coast west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antibes">Antibes</a>, near the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegitna">Aegitna</a>, probably around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandelieu-la-napoule">Mandelieu</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannes">Cannes</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> tells that they attacked Roman envoys landing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegitna">Aegitna</a> and wounded one of them.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 154 BCE the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-opimius">Quintus Opimius</a> marched against them, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegitna">Aegitna</a> and defeated them and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/deciates">Deciates</a>. Their land was given to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Massalia</a> and later absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-narbonensis">Gallia Narbonensis</a>, where the Roman colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frejus">Forum Julii</a> (Fréjus) was founded nearby.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 300 BCE – 154 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:2.91%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 154 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ligurian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-227&amp;focus=oxybii" aria-label="Oxybii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4765 525 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Oxybii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5085 781h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5085 781h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-227&amp;focus=oxybii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

